    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Elegantly Wasted is the tenth studio album by INXS, released in 1997 on Mercury and produced by Bruce Fairbairn and Andrew Farriss. Musically, it leans into polished rock and pop with an alternative edge, balancing sleek hooks, glossy production, and the band’s familiar mix of swagger and atmosphere.\n\nThe album arrived after a period of creative uncertainty and became the final INXS studio record recorded with Michael Hutchence before his death later that year, giving it added historical weight. Its title track was issued as the lead single, and the album’s set of songs—including “Show Me (Cherry Baby),” “Don’t Lose Your Head,” and “Girl on Fire”—captures the band working in a more streamlined, radio-friendly mode while still sounding unmistakably like INXS.",
